  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>403</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>404</mn></math> be two arithmetic progressions. Then the sum, of the common terms in them, is equal to_________"
  },
